# Picly environment (copy to .env for local dev — see note below)
#
# ├─ backend/  → Hono (auth + in-app update manifest)
# ├─ web/      → landing page (static, served via Docker/nginx)
# └─ desktop/  → Electron app (fully local; backend only for auth + update)
#
# NOTE: nothing auto-loads this file (no dotenv, Docker doesn't read it). Treat
# it as a reference; export vars manually or pass them to `docker compose run`.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BACKEND (backend/src)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JWT signing secret for auth tokens. REQUIRED in production — generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# If unset, an ephemeral secret is used (tokens invalidate on every restart).
JWT_SECRET=

# Where the SQLite DB lives. Default /data/picly.db (Docker volume).
DB_PATH=/data/picly.db

# Backend listen port (default 9999). Docker maps 127.0.0.1:9999 -> container.
PORT=9999

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DESKTOP APP (desktop/src/main)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the backend the desktop app talks to (auth + in-app update).
# Local dev: leave empty → falls back to http://localhost:9999 (Docker).
# Production/VPS: point to the deployed backend, e.g.
#   PICLY_API_URL=https://api.picly.app
# Read at RUNTIME by the Electron main process (not baked in at build time).
# PICLY_API_URL=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DOCKER (docker-compose.yml)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override the in-app update manifest without rebuilding the backend image
# (see backend/src/update.ts for the compile-in defaults).
# PICLY_LATEST_VERSION=1.1.0
# PICLY_UPDATE_URL=https://github.com/rizkhal/picly/releases/latest
